#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The Biggest MISTAKES Beginners Make on Their First Candle — image-visuals, v6.3 mix.
TH ~12% (hook/CTA/outro + single section transitions), still ~49%, video-clip(live/broll) ~28%, split ~10%.
MrBeast hook (title at END), ebook CTA <1:30, topics IN ORDER (kit promise -> what's in the kit -> melting ->
dye+fragrance -> pouring+topping up -> trimming+pretty finish), retention beats, subscribe+next outro.
Recurring subjects use subj= so the SAME object is reused across shots (hero_candle, kit)."""
import os,sys; sys.path.insert(0,os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))); from buildlib import *
start("The Biggest MISTAKES Beginners Make on Their First Candle")

# ===== HOOK (MrBeast — title said at the END) =====
th("Almost every beginner ruins their very first candle the same few ways.","bench")
full("a first-timer's soy candle with a deep sinkhole and an ugly tunnel down the middle","Sinkholes. Tunnels. Frosting. A wick that drowns. I have made every single one.","close-up")
live("a cheap candle burning with a deep tunnel, hard wax stuck high around the edge","the small flame sits low in a deep tunnel of leftover wax","A tunnel like this wastes half the candle you worked so hard to make.")
th("Here are the biggest first-candle mistakes, and exactly how to dodge them.","kitchen")
full("a few flawed beginner candles lined up, one frosted, one sunken, one cracked","Most of these come down to about six simple things. Every one is fixable.","wide")
th("Stay to the very end for the one mistake that catches almost everyone.","shelf")
full("a beautiful finished soy candle topped with a few dried flower petals, glowing softly","Get them right, and your very first candle can honestly look like this.","close-up",subj="hero_candle")

# ===== EBOOK CTA (within 1:30) =====
book("And every fix here is in my book, The Three Dollar Luxury Candle.","shelf")
full("the book beside a tidy beginner candle setup on the workbench","The beginner chapter walks through every mistake in this video, step by step.","close-up")

# ===== TOPIC 1: THE SIMPLE KIT PROMISE (a batch of five) =====
th("First, the good news. One basic kit makes about five candles.","bench")
full("a beginner candle-making starter kit box with soy wax, wicks, jars and a fragrance bottle","A simple starter kit has everything for your first batch of five.","close-up",subj="kit")
full("five empty glass candle jars lined up in a row ready to be filled","Five little jars. By the end of this, all five will be finished candles.","wide")
split("Mistake one is buying random supplies that do not work together.","a messy pile of mismatched candle-making bits and bottles","bench","left")
full("a matched soy wax bag, wick and jar taken from one kit","A matched kit removes the biggest beginner trap: parts that fight each other.","close-up",subj="kit")
live("the starter kit sitting open on the bench in soft window light","light shifts gently across the open kit on the bench","Start with one kit, make five, and learn the whole process once.",subj="kit")

# ===== TOPIC 2: WHAT'S IN THE KIT =====
th("So what is actually inside? Let us open it up.","packing")
full("an open kit showing a bag of soy wax flakes, wicks, jars, a fragrance bottle and stickers","Soy wax, wicks, jars, a little fragrance oil, and usually some labels.","close-up",subj="kit")
live("a bag of soft white soy wax flakes resting on the workbench","the soft white flakes shift and settle inside the bag","Soy wax melts low and cleans up with soap and water. Perfect for a first try.")
full("a few pre-tabbed candle wicks with little metal bases","Pre-tabbed wicks save you the fiddly setup. You just centre them and go.","close-up")
split("Mistake two is using the wrong wick size for the jar.","a tiny wick lost in a too-wide candle jar","bench","right")
full("a single wick standing dead-centre in an empty jar","Use the wick the kit gives you, kept centred, and most problems vanish.","close-up")
br("clips a wick into a small centring bar laid across the top of a jar","A little bar across the top holds the wick straight while the wax sets.")
full("a wick standing perfectly straight and centred in an empty glass jar","Centred wick, standing straight. This one step prevents so much heartbreak.","close-up")
live("an empty prepared jar with a centred wick waiting on the bench","the centred wick stands still in the empty jar","Get the jar prepped first, before a drop of wax is melted.")

# ===== TOPIC 3: MELTING THE WAX (don't fuss the temperature yet) =====
th("Now we melt the wax. And here is where beginners panic.","kitchen")
full("soy wax flakes melting in a metal jug sat inside a pot of water on the stove","Melt the wax gently in a jug sitting in hot water. Low and slow.","close-up")
live("soy wax flakes slowly turning into clear melted liquid in a jug over water","the white flakes slowly melt down into clear liquid wax","Watch it go from flakes to clear. It is honestly really relaxing.")
split("Mistake three is overheating wax on direct high heat.","wax smoking in a dry pan on a bare burner","kitchen","left")
full("a kitchen thermometer resting in a jug of gently melted wax","Do not stress the exact temperature yet. Just never let it smoke.","close-up")
live("melted wax sitting calmly in a jug, just off the heat","a faint heat shimmer rises over the still melted wax","Melt it, lift it off the heat, and let it cool for a couple of minutes.")
live("steam rising gently off a jug of melted wax cooling on the bench","faint steam drifts up off the cooling wax","Letting it cool a little before pouring is half the secret. Do not rush.")

# ===== TOPIC 4: ADDING DYE AND FRAGRANCE =====
th("Next, the fun part. Colour and scent.","bench")
full("a small bottle of candle fragrance oil being measured beside a jug of melted wax","Stir your fragrance in while the wax is melted, but not piping hot.","close-up")
live("fragrance oil being poured and stirred into melted wax in a jug","the oil swirls in and blends through the melted wax","Stir gently for a full minute so the scent actually binds to the wax.")
split("Mistake four is dumping in far too much fragrance.","fragrance oil flooding over the top of a jug of wax","bench","right")
full("a small measuring cup holding a modest amount of fragrance oil","More is not stronger. Too much just sweats out and will not set properly.","close-up")
full("a single tiny drop of liquid candle dye going into melted wax","For colour, one drop of dye is plenty. You can add more, never less.","close-up")
live("melted wax turning a soft even pastel colour as dye blends in","the colour spreads slowly and evenly through the wax","One drop, stirred well, gives you this soft even colour.")
live("two jugs of melted wax in two gentle colours side by side","the two coloured waxes swirl gently in their jugs","Keep colours soft and natural. Pastels always look more expensive than neon.")

# ===== TOPIC 5: POURING AND TOPPING UP =====
th("Now we pour. Slow and steady wins here.","kitchen")
full("melted wax being poured slowly into a prepared jar with a centred wick","Let the wax cool a touch, then pour slowly into your prepared jar.","close-up")
live("melted wax filling a glass jar steadily around a centred wick","the wax level rises smoothly around the standing wick","Pour in one smooth go, and keep that wick standing straight up.")
split("Mistake five is pouring wax that is still far too hot.","a cracked, sunken candle top from pouring too hot","kitchen","left")
live("a freshly poured candle cooling quietly on the bench","the surface of the fresh candle slowly firms up as it cools","Too hot, and you get sinkholes and cracks. A little patience fixes both.")
full("a setting candle with a small dip forming in the surface near the wick","Soy almost always dips a little as it cools. That part is completely normal.","close-up")
full("a small jug of saved melted wax kept aside for a second pour","This is why you save a little wax back. A second thin pour fixes the dip.","close-up")
live("a thin top-up layer of wax smoothing over a slightly sunken candle top","the surface fills in and settles perfectly level","A small top-up pour, and the surface goes flat and smooth again.")
br("gently taps the side of a freshly poured jar to release trapped air bubbles","Tap the jar gently after pouring to let little air bubbles rise and escape.")

# ===== TOPIC 6: TRIMMING WICKS + THE PRETTY FINISH (the end mistake) =====
th("And here is the one almost everyone gets wrong.","shelf")
full("a candle burning with a long untrimmed wick and a tall smoky flame","Mistake six. Burning it with a long wick gives you soot and a huge flame.","close-up")
br("trims a candle wick down to about a quarter inch with small scissors","Trim the wick to about a quarter inch before every single burn.")
split("No wick trimmer? Do not panic, scissors are completely fine.","ordinary kitchen scissors trimming a candle wick","bench","right")
full("a neatly trimmed short wick on a finished candle","A short wick gives a small, calm, clean flame. Every single time.","close-up",subj="hero_candle")
full("a finished candle being topped with a few pressed dried flower petals","And the pretty finish. A few dried petals on top make it feel special.","close-up",subj="hero_candle")
live("a finished petal-topped candle glowing with a small calm flame","the small flame glows gently above the dried petals","Lit, trimmed and topped with petals. Your first candle, done right.",subj="hero_candle")

# ===== BONUS: FROSTING & WET SPOTS (harmless 'mistakes') =====
full("a soy candle on a shelf with a few natural-looking surface quirks","A couple more things beginners always worry about, but really should not.","close-up")
split("Those white crystals on soy are called frosting. It is harmless.","a soy candle showing natural white frosting on the surface","window","left")
full("a close look at natural frosting across a soy candle top","Frosting is just soy being natural. It does not change how it burns at all.","close-up")
split("Those little bubbles on the glass are wet spots. Also harmless.","wet spots where wax has pulled away from the jar glass","window","right")
full("a jar candle with small wet spots showing against the glass","Wet spots are just wax pulling from the glass as it cools. Totally normal.","close-up")

# ===== BONUS: JAR & WAX CHOICE =====
full("a few different candle jars, a tin and a glass tumbler side by side","Almost any heat-safe glass or tin works. A wide jar just needs a bigger wick.","wide")
live("a hand setting a clean glass jar onto the workbench","a clean jar is set down gently on the bench","Reuse old candle jars too. Clean out the wax and they are good as new.")
split("Mistake seven is a jar that is too tall and narrow for the wick.","a tall narrow jar with a weak flame struggling down inside","bench","left")
full("a wide, gently tapered jar that lets a flame breathe","Pick a jar that is not too deep, so the flame gets enough air.","close-up")

# ===== BONUS: SCENT THROW TIPS =====
full("a candle with a wide even melt pool reaching the edge of the jar","Want it to actually fill the room? Start with the very first burn.","close-up")
live("a candle burning evenly with the wax pooling right out to the glass","the flame flickers gently as the melt pool widens to the glass","Let the first burn melt all the way to the edge. That sets the memory.")
split("Mistake eight is snuffing it out before the melt pool reaches the sides.","a candle with a small melt pool tunnelling early","bench","right")
full("a candle burning with a full melt pool right out to the glass","A full melt pool on burn one means no tunnelling for the whole candle.","close-up")
live("a candle glowing on a side table filling a cozy room with soft light","the flame flickers gently, warm light filling the room","Cure it, trim it, burn it fully, and the scent will carry beautifully.")

# ===== BONUS: GIFTING / PACKAGING =====
full("a finished candle with a simple kraft label and a little ribbon","Add a plain label and a ribbon and a homemade candle becomes a real gift.","close-up",subj="hero_candle")
live("a gift-wrapped candle tied with twine resting on the bench","the little candle sits wrapped and ready to give","Five candles from one kit makes five thoughtful, almost-free presents.")
live("three petal-topped candles boxed up neatly as a little gift set","light shifts softly across the boxed gift set of candles","Box a few together and you have a gift set that looks shop-bought.")

# ===== BONUS: SAFETY (calm, reassuring) =====
full("a lit candle sitting safely on a clear flat heatproof surface","Quick safety, because it matters. Burn on a flat heatproof surface, away from clutter.","close-up")
split("Mistake nine is leaving a candle burning unattended.","an unattended candle burning near a curtain","kitchen","left")
full("a candle being gently snuffed out with a small lid","Never leave a flame alone, and snuff it rather than blowing wax everywhere.","close-up")
live("a thin ribbon of smoke rising from a just-snuffed wick","a soft ribbon of smoke curls up from the wick","Snuffing keeps the wick centred and stops that hot-wax splatter.")
full("a candle that has burned down to about a centimetre of wax left","Stop burning when about a centimetre of wax is left, so the jar never overheats.","close-up")

# ===== BONUS: TROUBLESHOOTING Q&A =====
full("a candle with a wick gone slightly off-centre after setting","If your wick drifts off-centre, warm the top gently and nudge it straight.","close-up")
split("My candle tunnelled. Can I save it? Usually, yes.","a tunnelled candle being rescued","bench","right")
live("a hairdryer-warmed candle top melting smooth and level again","the uneven surface softens and melts back to level","Warm the whole top until it levels out, then let it set flat again.")
full("a candle with a sooty black mark climbing the inside of the glass","Black soot on the glass almost always means the wick was too long.","close-up")
full("a clean jar wall beside a sooty one, side by side","Trim the wick and that soot simply stops. It really is that simple.","close-up")

# ===== BONUS: LAYERING COLOUR & SIMPLE UPGRADES =====
full("a candle with two soft colour layers set one above the other","Once you are comfortable, try two soft colour layers for a simple upgrade.","close-up")
live("a second colour of wax being poured over a set first layer","the new colour settles in a clean band over the first","Let the first layer set, then pour the next. Clean, soft bands every time.")
split("Mistake ten is pouring the next layer while the first is liquid.","two candle colours bleeding messily into each other","kitchen","left")
full("a neat two-tone candle with a crisp line between the colours","Patience between layers gives you that crisp, intentional line.","close-up")
full("a candle with a single dried flower pressed against the glass","A single pressed flower on the inside of the glass looks gorgeous and costs nothing.","close-up")

# ===== BONUS: REUSING WAX & VALUE =====
full("leftover wax scraps being saved in a small jar","Save every wax scrap. Beginners toss wax that could have been another candle.","close-up")
live("wax scraps melting back down together in a jug","the odd scraps melt back into one pool of wax","Melt your offcuts together for a free, one-of-a-kind candle later.")
full("five finished candles beside a single low price tag","Five candles from one cheap kit. The value here is honestly hard to beat.","wide")

# ===== CURING (relatability / patience) =====
th("Now the hardest mistake of all. Not waiting.","bench")
full("a row of fresh candles curing on a shelf with a small handwritten date label","Let them cure a few days before burning. The scent gets so much better.","wide")
live("finished candles resting on a curing shelf in soft window light","the candles sit quietly curing in the gentle light","Twenty four hours later, and yes, I have changed my outfit. They need patience.")
live("a cured candle being lit for the first time, a match brought to the wick","the match touches the wick and the flame catches and steadies","After a few days, that very first burn is absolutely worth the wait.")

